  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABIGPMug",
      "title": "feat(proxyd): new proxyd_http_request_by_method_duration_seconds metric",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 764,
      "body": "Signed-off-by: Yashvardhan Kukreja <yashvardhan@oplabs.co>\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds `proxyd_http_request_by_method_duration_seconds`, a per-method summary of HTTP JSON-RPC latency. The existing `proxyd_http_request_duration_seconds` series is unchanged. It still times every HTTP request, including GET /healthz and WebSocket connections, with no method_name label.\r\n\r\n`method_name` is bounded by `rpc_method_mappings`. Batches are labeled `<batch>`, requests rejected before a method is known are labeled `unknown`, and `proxyd_healthz` keeps its own name. WebSocket connections and `GET /healthz` are excluded.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- [ ] `go test ./ -run 'TestHTTPRequestByMethodDuration|TestHTTPRequestMethodLabel'`\r\n- [ ] Confirm the new series appears on `/metrics` for a single call, a batch, and a rejected request, and that an unlisted method increments `method_not_allowed` rather than creating a new series.\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-13T04:30:31Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 241,
      "deletions": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOL-xLQ88AAAABIGaxxQ",
      "title": "feat(proxyd): tx_validation_middleware: configurable max connections per host and max idle connections",
      "author": "yashvardhan-kukreja",
      "number": 765,
      "body": "Signed-off-by: Yashvardhan Kukreja <yashvardhan@oplabs.co>\r\n\r\n<!-- Contributions welcome! See https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/.github/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md -->\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\nThe tx validation middleware's HTTP client hardcodes `MaxConnsPerHost=10`. DUe to this, during traffic bursts, a few slow validation calls can fill every connection, and later requests queue behind them.\r\n\r\nThe validation timeout starts before the request is sent, so time spent waiting for a connection counts against it. Under load, queued requests reach the validation service with little time left. They either time out, failing open or closed depending on `fail_open`, or add seconds of latency to tx submission, even when the validation service itself responds quickly.\r\n\r\n`MaxIdleConnsPerHost` was also unset, so Go's default of 2 applied. After each burst, all but 2 connections were closed and had to be re-dialed on the next one.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n- Add `max_conns_per_host` and `max_idle_conns` to `[tx_validation_middleware]`. Both default to **30**, up from 10, and unset or non-positive values fall back to the default.\r\n- Set `MaxIdleConnsPerHost` to `max_idle_conns`. The client only talks to a single host, so the two limits are equivalent.\r\n- Document the new options in `example.config.toml`.\r\n\r\n### Upgrade notes\r\n- **No config changes are required.** Existing deployments get the higher defaults automatically.\r\n- **Validation service load:** the service may now receive up to 30 concurrent requests per proxyd instance. Operators whose service can't handle that can lower `max_conns_per_host`.\r\n- **Timeout behavior is unchanged:** time spent waiting for a connection still counts against `timeout_seconds`.\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/infra",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-13T04:57:20Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 58,
      "deletions": 13
    }
  ],
